A||||18||Richard Parnell||Marvel Mystery Oil||||5||
Z||000000||Richard Parnell||11-20-2000||01:40 PM||||Any one ever heard of Marvel Mystery Oil?  My mechanic squirted into my engine before install because it had been sitting for 4 years.  After letting sit overnught he started it up, it blew out a bunch of crud and has run smooth and clean ever since.  He puts it into his oil (just a little) and 8 ounces per tank of gas.  It keeps everything clean and smooth.||||reg||5
Z||000001||KRMFiero||11-20-2000||03:40 PM||||I love that stuff, anytime a piston freeses o my outboard motors i put some in let it sit, pull the cord and starts right up again... right now my fiero doest run correctly and for the winter i put 1/8 a can in the gas, 3/4 in the oil then the rest in the cyliners just so there is no chance of them freesing up||||reg||1
Z||000002||PatrickB||11-20-2000||04:48 PM||||I put a 16 ounce bottle(I think its 16) in with every oil change.  I love that stuff. In my old talon I put it in and a week later it got rid of my lifter noise.  Im a little scared to put it into my fuel though.<P>My flight instructor also used to put it in his plane in the oil and the fuel.  But he also put some kind of acid in the fuel to keep everything clean also.||||reg||14
Z||000003||TheFiero64||11-20-2000||05:19 PM||||Marvel Mystery Oil is great. I use it all the time. I know a lot of old timers that swear by the stuff. It has been around for ever.<P>------------------<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000004||rockcrawl||11-20-2000||06:28 PM||||My dad is one of those old-timers that swears by this stuff. Every time he hears an engine noise, he says "Put a little Marvel Mystery Oil in there". I can personally vouch for its ability to quiet a noisey valve train, it does work in some cases.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Spyder||11-20-2000||06:46 PM||||I used it on my Z to stop lifter knocking.<BR>IT WORKED!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||webbee||11-20-2000||07:05 PM||||Ditto, MMO rules. <P>You can make a good assembly lube by mixing MMO and white grease together. Basically you want to thin the grease a bit. It makes for nicely broken in rings, bearings and super clean engine interiors.<P>I always use it to break in any engine I build. I also run a qt of MMO in place of a regular qt of oil.  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||bHooper||11-20-2000||10:55 PM||||so, are you saying there are are no drawbacks to this stuff?  <P>wheres ogre for counter point, when you need him?<P>i guess i will have to give it a try, then.<P>does it work well with antifreeze?  jk<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000008||Richard Parnell||11-21-2000||01:34 AM||||I know you can use it the gas (8 fl oz per tank approx,), oil 1 qt out of the total qts required and in the tranny whatever it takes to top off.  I will us eit in all my cars and anyones car i work on. i was amazed and am sold on it.  ||||reg||14
Z||000009||Oreif||11-21-2000||01:45 AM||||So where do I find it? Auto parts stores? Kmart?||||reg||5
Z||000010||mrfiero||11-21-2000||02:08 AM||||K-Mart, Wal-Mart, Auto Zone, etc.  Just about every store carries this stuff.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||RossT||11-21-2000||02:09 AM||||Walmart has it. (in a red and black metal can) I use a simular product called "Seafoam". I put it in the snowblower's oil to help get rid of all the water that builds up in the oil (no air filter on these things)  I also use it in the gas as an injector cleaner and fuel stabilizer (stored stuff).  I also use it in the oil of all my cars about once a year.  It help clean alot of the carbon and gunk out that regular oil changes do not get.  <P>Seafoam and mystery oil are the only additives that my mechanic will touch!!<p>[This message has been edited by RossT (edited 11-21-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||HYPTNOTiSE||11-21-2000||02:45 AM||||At my used car dealership, every new car we get gets a squirt in the engine and a squirt in the gas tank, WE SWARE by the stuff! We photo copied the bottle and thumb tacked it to the wall in the storage closet.  Never heard anything bad about it.  So what's the real "mystery" behind this stuff, is it sent from God?<P><P>------------------<BR>       Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ Nitrous<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tcac.net/~daddyg/hypsig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||BAM-BAM||11-21-2000||07:53 AM||||  You can use this stuff in the tranny? Let me know, cause I'm having a couple small anomalies show up from time to time, maybe it will help. Oh by the way, I'm talking about my GP not my Fiero.<BR>  <BR>   Peace, BAM OUT!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by BAM-BAM (edited 11-21-2000).]||||reg||7
Z||000014||Mattsfiero||11-22-2000||11:24 AM||||MMO is awsome. I use it all the time and keep aslot in stock at home. I will warn about one thing don't use it consitently in your fuel system. Just like anything else you don't want to clean it out to the point where anything in the fuel system dries out but to add it once in awhile instead of Fuel system cleaner is a great Idea.<P>------------------<BR>Matt<BR>85 custom coupe<BR>Mattsfiero@excite.com<BR>www.anglefire.com/ma3/mattsfiero||||reg||4
Z||000015||PatrickB||11-22-2000||03:19 PM||||Haha has anyone noticed that they switched from the metal can to a plastic bottle?  I am totally heartbroken.||||reg||9
Z||000016||Richard Parnell||11-22-2000||03:58 PM||||If you buy it by the gallon it still comes in the metal can.  I cracked me up the first time I saw it.  It looked like something from the 1920s. But it sure works.||||reg||7
Z||000017||JohnnyK||11-23-2000||10:27 PM||||I went looking for this stuff, but the MMO I found was in a red plastic bottle and it said "Fuel Additive".. Is there two types? One for oil and one for fuel? Or can you put the fuel additive in the oil?||||reg||1
Z||000018||MrPBody||11-23-2000||10:36 PM||||At the shop where I used to work, someone told me that MMO was used as upper cylinder lubricant in old -- I mean **old**, like pre-WW2 -- aircraft engines, in the days before pressure lubrication systems.  If true, that would explain the hokey name and old-style graphics.<P>I think it's great stuff, too.<BR>||||reg||1
